      {
        "id": 181476,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-08-24T13:59:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"LewdDolphin21\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lewddolphin21/48/1893_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LewdDolphin21:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Powerhound_2000 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>His issue wasn't about limiting the drugs but about how you stopped the massive damage from when he flips and would get a damage boost due to the victims in the safe house. &nbsp;In my case on the turn he flipped I put a Forced Entry on top so that post flip he did not get a damage boost.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSorry, misunderstood.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>No harm done and no offence taken! More help is better than less!</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:06:14.648Z",
